---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";

// Privacy policy for Darktier Studios apps (Google Play requires a public,
// non-geofenced policy URL for every listing) and for this website.
// Keep it truthful: the apps collect nothing, so the policy says so.
const effective = "September 17, 2026";
// The address Google Play lists as the developer contact. Change here only.
const contact = "sheibeck@gmail.com";
---
<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Darktier Studios privacy policy — our apps collect no personal data. Game saves stay on your device. Nothing is sent anywhere."
>
  <div class="container">
    <section style="padding:84px 0 28px">
      <p class="kicker">Darktier Studios · legal</p>
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(40px,6vw,72px);line-height:1.04;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0 0 0 -0.06em">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="privacy-meta">Effective {effective} · {site.legalName}, {site.location}</p>
    </section>

    <article class="privacy">
      <p class="privacy-lede">
        The short version: <strong>we don't collect your data.</strong> Not your name, not your email,
        not your location, not how you play. Our games run entirely on your device, and what happens
        in the dungeon stays in the dungeon.
      </p>

      <h2>Who this covers</h2>
      <p>
        This policy applies to mobile apps published by {site.legalName} on Google Play — currently
        <strong>Delve, Die, Repeat</strong> (package <code>com.darktierstudios.delvedierepeat</code>) — and to
        this website, <a href={site.url}>{site.url}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Our apps</h2>
      <h3>Data we collect</h3>
      <p>None. Our apps do not collect, transmit, sell, or share any personal or device data. Specifically, they do not collect:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Personal information (name, email address, user IDs, phone number, address)</li>
        <li>Location data, precise or approximate</li>
        <li>Financial or payment information</li>
        <li>Contacts, calendar, photos, videos, audio, or files</li>
        <li>App activity, gameplay analytics, or crash and diagnostic reports</li>
        <li>Device identifiers or the Android Advertising ID</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Data stored on your device</h3>
      <p>
        The game keeps a small amount of data on your phone so it works: your current run, the graveyard of
        adventurers who came before it, and your settings. This data never leaves your device, is never
        sent to us or to anyone else, and is removed when you uninstall the app.
      </p>

      <h3>No accounts, no network, no third parties</h3>
      <p>
        Our apps require no account and work fully offline. They contain no advertising, analytics,
        crash-reporting, or social SDKs, and make no network requests of their own. The only third party
        involved is Google Play, which handles your purchase and installation under
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's privacy policy</a>;
        we receive no personal information from that transaction.
      </p>

      <h3>Permissions</h3>
      <p>
        Our apps do not request access to your location, contacts, camera, microphone, storage, or any other
        permission-gated data.
      </p>

      <h3>Children</h3>
      <p>
        Our apps are suitable for general audiences and collect no data from anyone, including children
        under 13. Because nothing is collected, there is nothing to review, correct, or delete.
      </p>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        The public pages of this site are static and set no tracking cookies. They do not use advertising
        or analytics services. The site is hosted on Google's Firebase platform, and the games catalog is
        loaded from Google's Firestore database; like any web host, Google may record standard server logs
        (such as your IP address and browser type) to deliver the pages, governed by
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's privacy policy</a>.
        We do not access or use those logs to identify you.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Since we hold no personal data about you, there is nothing for us to export, correct, or erase.
        Everything the app stores lives on your device under your control; uninstalling the app deletes it.
        If a future app ever changes that, this policy will change first.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If we update this policy, the new version will be posted at this address with a new effective date.
        Material changes to what an app collects will also be reflected in that app's Google Play listing.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a><br />
        {site.legalName} · {site.location}
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .privacy-meta {
    margin: 21px 0 0;
    font-size: 13px;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 55%, transparent);
  }
  .privacy {
    max-width: 66ch;
    padding: 0 0 84px;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 28px;
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 82%, transparent);
  }
  .privacy-lede {
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 32px;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 0 0 42px;
    padding: 24px 28px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-neutral-700);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-neutral-900) 45%, transparent);
  }
  .privacy h2 {
    margin: 42px 0 14px;
    font-size: 26px;
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }
  .privacy h3 {
    margin: 28px 0 8px;
    font-size: 13px;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  .privacy p { margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .privacy ul { margin: 0 0 16px; padding-left: 22px; }
  .privacy li { margin: 4px 0; }
  .privacy a { color: var(--color-text); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .privacy a:hover { color: var(--color-accent); }
  .privacy code {
    font-size: 14px;
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-neutral-800) 80%, transparent);
  }
</style>
